# prismlauncher — #8's acceptance test. Needs `deb [...] sid contrib` added
# to sources.list.d (it's in Debian's contrib archive area, not main, so it
# won't even show up in `apt-cache search` until that's added). Also needed
# `scripts/lock-seeded.sh unlock` once to let a newer private Qt6 land under
# $PREFIX (the seeded/held system Qt6 was older than what sid's current
# prismlauncher packaging requires) — re-lock afterward.
#
# check-package.sh already correctly calls it tier=overlay (paths baked in
# under /etc/xdg, /usr/lib/jvm) — no new mechanism needed there. What #8
# actually proposed (a --gui flag) turned out to matter for a narrower
# reason than assumed: prefix-run.sh's plain overlay mode already passes
# through DISPLAY/WAYLAND_DISPLAY/XDG_RUNTIME_DIR by accident, because its
# base bind is the *entire* host / (`--ro-bind / /`) before overlaying
# /usr,/etc — rootfs mode replaces / outright and would NOT see the session
# without --gui's explicit $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR bind. --gui also refuses clearly
# with no session, which nothing did before.
#
# Verified for real, not just launched and assumed: logged into a Minecraft
# account and downloaded a modded instance through the actual GUI, running
# under this exact mechanism (tools/prefix-run.sh, unmodified aside from
# --gui) on a live Mobian/Phosh session.
package  prismlauncher
install  ok
tier     gui
verify   tools/prefix-run.sh --gui prismlauncher --version
note     needs `sid contrib` in sources.list.d and a one-time `lock-seeded.sh unlock`/`lock` for a newer Qt6; see #8
